# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the deployment root, and this repository's root holds
# four workspaces plus two Expo prebuild trees. The first attempt died with
# "Upload aborted" — `du` on node_modules alone could not finish inside five
# minutes, and apps/*/android contains Gradle transform paths long enough that
# git itself reports "Filename too long" when walking them.
#
# Only the website is being built here. Everything below is either regenerated
# on the build machine, belongs to a different workspace, or is a binary served
# from somewhere else entirely.

node_modules
.git

# Regenerated by the build.
.next
dist
backend/dist
web/.next

# Expo prebuild output: native Android and iOS projects, plus Gradle caches.
# Gigabytes, and nothing the Next.js site imports.
apps/*/android
apps/*/ios
apps/*/.expo

# The APKs are ~45 MB each and gitignored by design. app-download-section.tsx
# reads their GitHub Release URLs out of the committed manifest.json instead,
# and only falls back to a local file so that `build-apk.sh` alone still shows
# a working download on localhost. Uploading them would add 90 MB to every
# deployment for a path the deployed site never takes.
web/public/downloads/*.apk

# The archived React + Vite site. Not a workspace, not built, not served.
legacy-vite-site

# Local-only.
.env*
.vercel
*.log
sfgc-new-passwords.csv
